--- Scope / parity ---
Surface = native WinUI 3 port of web/src/components/data-display/BatteryDelta.tsx: a compact, purely
presentational battery state-of-charge change. New code (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/):
  - BatteryDelta.Model.cs (WinUI-free): BatteryDeltaRegistration (slug + the shared \uE83F battery glyph),
    BatteryDeltaVariant (Compact|Pair), BatteryDeltaTone (Positive|Negative|Neutral), BatteryDeltaModel
    (startPct/endPct/showIcon/variant props), BatteryDeltaDisplay, BatteryDeltaProjection (the web logic), and
    PII-safe BatteryDeltaDiagnostics (view.opened slug=BatteryDelta).
  - BatteryDelta.cs: a ContentControl that renders the inline icon+text row and binds to the projection.
  - TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/BatteryDeltaTests.cs: 34 headless tests (adapter/projection per state,
    sign/dash/arrow code points, number stringification, tone->brush map, a11y name, diagnostics, guards).
Parity decisions (web source is THE spec):
  - hasData requires both endpoints non-null AND finite; otherwise the muted em dash (U+2014) + aria
    t('battery.delta.unknown','Battery delta unknown'). Both branches always render.
  - delta = endPct-startPct; sign '+' / U+2212 minus (NOT a hyphen) / ''; magnitude = |delta|.
  - tone: rise => emerald (TsColorSuccessBrush), drop => amber (TsColorWarningBrush; a drained battery is the
    NORMAL drive outcome, so amber, never red), zero/no-data => muted (TsColorTextMutedBrush). The generic
    Core DeltaLogic was deliberately NOT reused: its Negative maps to danger/red and it is direction-aware.
  - compact = (delta==0 ? em dash : {sign}{magnitude}%); pair = {startPct}% -> {endPct}% (U+2192 arrow).
  - numbers reproduce the web raw template literal ${n} (shortest round-trippable invariant form, e.g. 78 stays
    "78", 12.5 stays "12.5"); verified double.ToString(InvariantCulture) == JS Number.toString for these values.
  - aria t('battery.delta.aria','Battery {{from}}% to {{to}}%') interpolated in code (react-i18next runtime).
    Both i18n keys are inline i18next defaults in the web source (absent from the shared catalog), so the exact
    keys + English fallbacks resolve through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade (PassthroughLocalizer in tests).
  - colour split mirrors the web: data branch tones only the TEXT (icon inherits the ambient currentColor); the
    no-data branch mutes both. Icon is AccessibilityView.Raw (web aria-hidden); the surface carries the single
    composed aria-label; tabular-nums has no TextBlock-level WinUI equivalent (visual-only, documented).
No async data source (parent row owns fetching) => no loading/error/stale/offline chrome, same precedent as
shared-surfaces/0003 VisuallyHidden and feature-views BatteryPill (both prop-driven presentational surfaces).

